  "problem": "In an environmental study, the water level in a reservoir (in $m$) after $t$ hours is given by the function $W(t).$ The values of $W(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| **$t$** | $0.8$ | $1.0$ | $1.2$ | $1.4$ | $1.6$ | $1.8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$W(t)$** | $5.6$ | $5.3$ | $5.0$ | $4.7$ | $4.2$ | $3.9$ |\n\nApproximate the reservoir\u2019s water level's instantaneous rate of change at $t=1.4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=0.2.$\n\nThe reservoir\u2019s water level at $t=1.4$ is decreasing at approximately \n{{field-1}} $m$ per hour.",
